I really wouldn't count on an AoLS. My experience is that you can get
quite a lot of touch-of-death messages in encounters with the Wizard
(and other major spell-casting foes); Double Trouble events increase
that risk.

To look back at the original question; oilskin as a countermeasure
for sea-food attacks is hardly necessary, even on the Plane of Water.
And I say that for the more "difficult" condition of doing the game
even with reduce speed (due to my burdeness), and staying comparably
a long time on the planes because I don't (levitation-)short-cut the
level. In case you're unlucky and get grabbed, a single zap from a
wand of teleportation at the monster solves the issue trivially and
without any risk (well, stay away from electric eels, anyway).

To sum up; the safety from an instant death risk of a MR-less late
game is nothing I would give up. To "play it save", always have MR
in the late game, and one that comes from a source that cannot be
stolen.

